  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ChalkQL 0.5 introduces standing queries and experimental incremental view maintenance (IVM), alongside more responsive planning, improved temporal semantics and stricter policy enforcement.\n\n      - **Standing views:** Keep SQL results current as inputs change, with cursors that expose only changed rows. Experimental IVM propagates changes through supported query plans instead of recomputing entire results.\n      - **Planning and refresh:** Plan asynchronously off the refresh path, control when new plans take effect with `PlanAsync` and `PlanNow()`, and observe planning decisions.\n      - **SQL enhancements:** Add rollups, seek-based as-of joins, single-evaluation CTEs, `CURRENT_TIME` and `LOCALTIME`, and additional date/time/timestamp casts.\n      - **Correctness and security:** Improve temporal conformance, make zoned-timestamp parsing independent of the machine's time zone, inherit path visibility from parents by default, and tighten safeguards around statistical columns.\n      - **Compatibility:** Some query and entitlement configurations whose behaviour was unspecified in 0.4 are now explicitly supported or rejected. Query plans may change due to improved planner optimisations and source-pushdown conformance. Incremental floating-point aggregation does not yet use compensated summation, so results may differ slightly from full recomputation.\n      - **Licence:** Changed to Elastic License 2.0 (ELv2). See the README for permitted-use details.\n      \n      Full release notes:\n      https://github.com/markhammond/chalkql/releases/tag/v0.5",
